{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a national dog owner licensing & education framework\u00a0",
        "additional_details": "Dog ownership is a privilege & responsibility. Dogs Trust & RSPCA found 96% of owners consider themselves responsible, yet 86% of the public have experienced irresponsible ownership, a dangerous mismatch in understanding & culture. Dog bites cost our NHS over \u00a3777 million in 2020. A national approach saves money, closes gaps in knowledge, funds education, enforcement & helps unify a supported culture of responsible ownership, preventing serious problems & expensive bite incidents.",
        "background": "We would like Government to introduce a national dog owner licensing & education scheme, with income ring-fenced for enforcement, improved data systems & support the rescue sector. Traceability & accountability helps owners understand their responsibilities, plus protects dogs, owners & communities.",
